+   "source": [
+    "# Simplified Pipeline — Outer Skin/Skull Surface Only\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**v2 — clean rewrite matching the reviewed pipeline diagram.** Functionally\n",
+    "the same validated pipeline as `CPD_TPS_Skin_Only_Registration.ipynb` (same\n",
+    "stage math, same PID-based external-surface extraction, same do-no-harm\n",
+    "safeguard), reorganized so the notebook's structure and markdown follow the\n",
+    "diagram below one-to-one. Two implementation stages (0.5 and 6.5) exist that\n",
+    "aren't drawn in the diagram — they're load-bearing fixes for bugs found while\n",
+    "building the first version, explained where they appear below, not scope\n",
+    "creep.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Change from the full pipeline:** brain and internal structures are not\n",
+    "warped — they stay at their original template coordinates. Only the outer\n",
+    "skin/skull surface is registered. Everything else (normalization,\n",
+    "registration stages, validation, final save) is unchanged.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "Template .k (skull+brain) ─┐\n",
+    "                             ├─ split: EXTRACT outer skin/skull surface only\n",
+    "SAM3D landmarks (subject) ──┘   (brain + internal parts set aside, untouched)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 0 — Center + resize\n",
+    "   Center both point sets at centroid, scale template to match subject\n",
+    "   bounding-box diagonal. (same as before)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 1 — PCA coarse pre-alignment\n",
+    "   Align principal axes (4-way sign-flip disambiguation) to give CPD\n",
+    "   a correct starting pose, avoiding symmetric local-minima convergence.\n",
+    "   (same as before)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 2 — Rigid CPD\n",
+    "   Rotation + isotropic scale + translation, refined from the PCA init.\n",
+    "   (same as before)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 3 — Affine CPD\n",
+    "   General linear map (anisotropic scale + shear) on top of rigid result.\n",
+    "   (same as before)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 4 — Non-rigid CPD\n",
+    "   Deformable point-set registration on the outer-surface landmark subset\n",
+    "   (subsampled for tractable O(N·M) cost). Produces sparse displacement\n",
+    "   field at landmark points only.\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 5 — TPS propagation (SCOPE REDUCED)\n",
+    "   Fit TPS on the Stage-4 landmark displacements, evaluate at every node\n",
+    "   of the DENSE OUTER SKIN/SKULL SURFACE only — not the brain, not any\n",
+    "   internal structure. Brain/internal nodes are excluded from this step\n",
+    "   entirely and simply carry over unchanged from the template.\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "[REMOVED for this version] Cavity-constraint / SDF correction\n",
+    "   Not needed — with the brain untouched, there's no brain-outside-skull\n",
+    "   violation to fix. Reintroduce this stage once brain-filling is added\n",
+    "   back in the full pipeline.\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 6 — Non-rigid ICP refinement\n",
+    "   Local polish of the warped outer surface against denser SAM3D surface\n",
+    "   detail, if available (Amberg-style, template topology preserved).\n",
+    "   (same as before — this only ever touched the outer surface anyway)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Stage 7 — Validation\n",
+    "   Symmetric NN / Chamfer / Hausdorff distance between warped skin\n",
+    "   surface and subject data, tracked stage-by-stage.\n",
+    "   k_mesh_qa.py check on the final .k (inverted elements, zero-area\n",
+    "   shells, coincident nodes).\n",
+    "   (same as before)\n",
+    "        │\n",
+    "        ▼\n",
+    "Final output\n",
+    "   Node coordinates updated for outer skin/skull surface only.\n",
+    "   Brain + all other internal parts: original template coordinates,\n",
+    "   unchanged. Element connectivity/topology/PIDs preserved throughout.\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Not drawn above, but present in this notebook (carried over from the\n",
+    "validated v1 build — see `CHANGELOG.md`):**\n",
+    "- **Stage 0.5 — landmark subsampling.** CPD cost is O(N·M) per iteration, so\n",
+    "  registration runs on a bounded farthest-point-sampled subset; Stage 5's TPS\n",
+    "  propagates the result back to the full dense surface.\n",
+    "- **Stage 6.5 — confidence-damped blend (do-no-harm safeguard).** Without it,\n",
+    "  regions with no real subject correspondence (e.g. ear/mastoid, missing scan\n",
+    "  coverage) can get a wild residual displacement from CPD/TPS/ICP that is\n",
+    "  *worse* than just leaving the point at its original template position. This\n",
+    "  stage blends toward whichever of (warped, original) is actually closer to\n",
+    "  the subject surface, spatially smoothed so mesh-adjacent points don't get\n",
+    "  wildly different treatment (that mismatch was the literal cause of visible\n",
+    "  spikes through the mesh in an earlier version). See `CHANGELOG.md` for the\n",
+    "  two bugs found and fixed in this stage.\n",
+    "- **Full skull bone volume + frozen boundary nodes.** The true external\n",
+    "  (skin-facing) surface drives the registration, but the skull's *solid* bone\n",
+    "  elements share nodes with both the external and internal shell faces —\n",
+    "  moving only the external face stretches every bone element between them.\n",
+    "  So Stage 5's TPS is evaluated on the full skull bone volume (external +\n",
